  "laneNotes": [
    "Eight families assigned, eight rows returned. Five completed, three stopped.",
    "Two of the three stops are one fact: both Texas nondisclosure families bind the same Statement of Inability binary, which lives in the human_source_returns custody that the corpus bootstrap does not install and no release carries.",
    "The third stop is a builder stop, not a source or legal one. nm_conviction-set binds all seven of its sources exactly and its legal inputs are settled; six of its seven documents are flat pleading pages whose blanks are typed underscore runs, which needs a third measurement mode this lane did not build.",
    "THREE FINDINGS THIS LANE FOUND AND DID NOT FIX, because each needs a shared host it does not own: the descriptor list carries nothing matching 'date of dismissal', so AOC-CR-287's offence table cannot be completed by any family; the caption capture on AOC-CR-287's identifier row returns neighbouring captions, falsely refusing the ZIP as a race field and the date of birth as a government identifier; and the flat-overlay path writes a single line, so a long address is refused in a cell the form draws 80 points deep for three lines.",
    "ONE DEFECT THIS LANE FOUND IN ITS OWN WORK AND FIXED: a NUL byte in the byte-proof lookup key meant every official-document write was silently skipped, so four families reported zero values proved while their finalizers reported 13, 6, 11 and 8. The counters read zero throughout, because a proof of nothing trips no counter.",
    "SOURCE-IDENTITY FINDING for the census: nc_146_dismissal_petition-set's alias official-form:AOC-CR-287 resolves to the INSTRUCTION SHEET (sha fe222704...) rather than to the petition (sha a8762293...). This lane binds by hash so it delivered the right bytes; a verifier following the alias will not."
  ],
